  "Many 'witches' were healers, midwives, or herbalists whose knowledge threatened both the church and early male medical establishment.",
  "In 1735, the British Witchcraft Act decriminalized witchcraft — declaring it an impossible crime. The last person imprisoned under it was Helen Duncan in 1944.",
