const magicTricks=[
  {cat:'mentalism',icon:'🧠',name:'The Book Test — Name Any Page',effect:'Ask someone to think of any page number in a book you have never seen. Tell them the first word on that page — correctly.',secret:'Before the gathering, open any book to a page number that ends in a repeating digital pattern (like page 111, 222, or any page divisible by 9). The key: for pages divisible by 9, the digital root always equals 9. Ask them to multiply their chosen number by 9, add the digits of the result until they get a single digit — it will always be 9. Assign 9 = "I" (9th letter). Then slowly reveal: "I see… the letter I. The first word begins with I." Or: pre-memorize page 108 of a book you own, hand it to them, and ask them to open to any page, multiply page by 9, reduce digits. Always 108-related.',type:'Mind Reading',difficulty:'★★☆'},
  {cat:'mentalism',icon:'🔮',name:'The Kreskin Force',effect:'Think of any number between 1 and 10. I already wrote mine down. We chose the same number.',secret:'Seven. Most people think of 7 when told "between 1 and 10." Psychologists put the rate above 30%. Write 7 on a folded paper before you begin. If they say 7, unfold it. If they don\'t, say "You thought 7 at first, didn\'t you?" — this is true about 60% of the time. If both fail, smoothly pivot: "Close — you\'re thinking of a number very near mine." This technique is called forcing and has never been fully explained.',type:'Mind Reading',difficulty:'★☆☆'},
  {cat:'mentalism',icon:'✉️',name:'The Sealed Envelope',effect:'You write a prediction, seal it in an envelope before the trick begins. At the end, the envelope reveals exactly what happened.',secret:'Write several possible outcomes on a small folded paper. After the result is revealed, subtly pull out the correct prediction with the others hidden in your palm. This is called "out" or "outs" — every professional has five for every trick. OR: write your prediction AFTER you\'ve seen their choice, but before the reveal, using a double-walled envelope (outer sealed, inner can be opened and re-sealed silently). The moment they announce their choice, you write quickly.',type:'Prediction',difficulty:'★★★'},
  {cat:'cards',icon:'🃏',name:'The Twenty-One Card Trick',effect:'Deal 21 cards into three columns of 7. Spectator thinks of a card. You deal and re-deal three times — and reveal their card.',secret:'After they indicate which column their card is in, gather the cards with that column always sandwiched in the middle. After three deals with three column-picks, their card is always the 11th card — the center. Count to card 11 and reveal it dramatically. This works by pure mathematics — it cannot fail if executed correctly. No skill required.',type:'Card Magic',difficulty:'★☆☆'},
  {cat:'cards',icon:'🂡',name:'The Rising Card',effect:'A card is chosen, shuffled back in the deck, which you then hold loosely. Slowly, impossibly, the chosen card rises from the deck.',secret:'When the card is returned, secretly separate the deck with a slight bend (called a "break") above the card. As you hold the deck, the little finger of your holding hand maintains this gap. To "raise" the card: press your thumb gently on the back of the deck while your fingers secretly push the chosen card up from below the break. It appears to rise on its own. Practice in front of a mirror for 10 minutes. You will fool everyone.',type:'Card Magic',difficulty:'★★☆'},
  {cat:'cards',icon:'♠️',name:'Read Their Mind Through the Deck',effect:'Spectator shuffles the deck and puts it face-down. You tell them the top card without looking.',secret:'The riffle shuffle leaves the original top card on top roughly 60% of the time. More reliably: use a "key card." Before they shuffle, secretly note the bottom card. After they cut the deck, their chosen card will be directly above your key card when they look through the face-up deck — you know their card before they say a word. This is the foundation of professional card reading.',type:'Card Magic',difficulty:'★★☆'},
  {cat:'coins',icon:'🪙',name:'The Vanishing Coin',effect:'A coin placed on the table passes through your hand and vanishes completely.',secret:'Place the coin on the table. Cover it with your right hand as if picking it up — but let it slip silently into your left palm (called a "French Drop"). Rub your "coin-filled" right hand and slowly open it: empty. The coin is secretly in your left hand. To make it "appear" elsewhere: drop it from your left hand into your collar, behind someone\'s ear, or into their closed fist while shaking hands. The misdirection — your right hand\'s theatrical opening — is everything.',type:'Coin Magic',difficulty:'★★☆'},
  {cat:'coins',icon:'💰',name:'The Coin Through the Table',effect:'You press a coin against the underside of a table — it passes through solid wood and appears in your other hand underneath.',secret:'Hold the coin against the underside of the table with your right hand. With your left hand on top, announce the coin will pass through. Tap three times. On the third tap, let the coin fall silently into your lap. Bring your right hand up (now empty) under the table while showing your left hand above is also empty. Reach under and "find" the coin in your lap, presenting it triumphantly. The noise of the tapping covers the sound of the coin dropping.',type:'Coin Magic',difficulty:'★★★'},
  {cat:'party',icon:'🍾',name:'The Unspillable Glass',effect:'You challenge anyone to move your glass of water using only a dollar bill. They cannot. You do it easily.',secret:'Fold the bill lengthwise into a tight pleat (accordion-fold it into about 8 ridges). The folded bill becomes stiff enough to slide under a full glass and move it. Challengers try with a flat bill, which buckles. You reveal the secret fold. The physics: distributed surface area from the pleats increases rigidity. The lesson: brains beat brawn.',type:'Party Trick',difficulty:'★☆☆'},
  {cat:'party',icon:'🔢',name:'The 1089 Prophecy',effect:'You already know what number they\'ll get — before they start.',secret:'Hand them a paper with "1089" written on it, face down. Ask them: think of any 3-digit number where the first and last digits differ by at least 2 (like 741). Reverse it (147). Subtract the smaller from the larger (741-147=594). Reverse the result (495). Add them (594+495=1089). ALWAYS. This is a mathematical constant that never fails. Tell them to flip the paper. The room goes quiet.',type:'Number Magic',difficulty:'★☆☆'},
  {cat:'party',icon:'🤚',name:'The Finger Through the Hole',effect:'You push your finger through a solid hole the size of a coin — impossibly.',secret:'Cut a small circle (coin-sized) from a piece of paper. Challenge anyone to push their finger through without tearing the paper. They cannot — the hole is too small. You take it, fold the paper in half through the center of the hole, and tear a small slit from the fold inward. Unfold: a slit extends outward from each side of the hole, allowing it to expand enough for a finger. Pure geometry, looks impossible.',type:'Party Trick',difficulty:'★☆☆'},
  {cat:'mentalism',icon:'🎨',name:'The Color Divination',effect:'You leave the room. Someone picks any color from a set of crayons. You return and name the color immediately.',secret:'Your secret confederate (a trusted friend in the audience) uses a simple code: they stand in the room with their arms crossed, they are seated with one leg crossed, they are pointing subtly — each posture means a color you\'ve pre-agreed. For a version without a confederate: when you take the crayon "to concentrate," hold it behind your back. Scratch it briefly against your thumbnail, then bring your hand to your temple to "think." Check your thumbnail — the color is there.',type:'Mind Reading',difficulty:'★★☆'},
  {cat:'party',icon:'⚖️',name:'The Impossible Bet',effect:'You bet anyone you can drink a shot glass of water through a solid playing card.',secret:'Poke a small hole in the card with your thumb, put the card over the glass, and drink through the hole using a straw or directly. The bet was technically winnable — you never said without modification. Classic bar trick. Variations: bet you can move a beer bottle using only a straw (fold the straw into an L, hook it under the bottle lip). The lesson every magician knows: the way a question is framed is not the only way it can be answered.',type:'Party Trick',difficulty:'★☆☆'},
  {cat:'coins',icon:'✨',name:'The Multiplying Coin',effect:'You hold one coin. It splits into four. Then back into one.',secret:'Begin with three coins secretly palmed in your right hand (classic palm, fingers slightly curled). Show one coin dramatically in your left. Transfer it to the right — as you do, release one coin from your palm at a time, catching them in your left as if multiplying. Reverse: collect them one by one into your right palm until you hold up a single coin. The key is slowness and theatricality — swift movements look like sleight of hand even when they\'re not.',type:'Coin Magic',difficulty:'★★★'},
  {cat:'mentalism',icon:'🌐',name:'Country Mind Reading',effect:'You tell someone the country they\'re thinking of.',secret:'Ask them to think of a country beginning with D. They almost certainly think of Denmark. (Germany is Deutschland in German but most English speakers don\'t go there first.) Then say "Now think of an animal beginning with the second letter of your country." They think of Elephant (E from dEnmark). "Now think of a color associated with that animal." Grey. Reveal: "You\'re thinking of a grey elephant from Denmark." Works on roughly 85% of people tested. The remainder thought of Dominican Republic or Djibouti — just say "I\'m getting Denmark — are you sure?" Confidence is the real trick.',type:'Mind Reading',difficulty:'★☆☆'},
];

