   lore:`Salt is the oldest magical protective substance in the world. The Romans salted their sacrifices — the word <em>salary</em> comes from it. In Jewish tradition a salt covenant was unbreakable. Across European folk magic, a line of salt at the threshold kept evil from entering. <strong>To share bread and salt with someone was a binding oath</strong> — you could not then betray them without supernatural consequence. Slavic hospitality still offers bread and salt to honored guests for this reason.`,
