    {name:'Owl',emoji:'🦉',element:'Air',tradition:'Celtic, Greek, Native American',
     headline:'The Watcher Between Worlds',
     lore:'Athena\'s sacred companion. The owl sees in darkness — and in every tradition that observed this, the same conclusion emerged: this creature moves between what is visible and what is hidden. In Celtic belief the owl (called the "Night Eagle") carried messages from the Otherworld. In many Native American traditions the owl brings word from ancestors. In ancient Greece it was the symbol of wisdom because it sees clearly when others are blind. A single white feather found at night is considered a direct message from someone who has passed.',
